    "sha": "20ef111cd41597ce7f0081d43e07ae88937c7574",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDIwZWYxMTFjZDQxNTk3Y2U3ZjAwODFkNDNlMDdhZTg4OTM3Yzc1NzQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T11:48:22Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T11:48:22Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(text): place typed text in a TrueType outline font as closed shapes\n\nAdd camcraft_geometry::outline_text: a bounds-checked TrueType reader\n(cmap 4/12, loca, glyf simple and composite, hmtx, OS/2 cap height),\nquadratic contours flattened within 0.005 mm, and a sketch of closed\nchains on the layer \"text\". Unreadable fonts, CFF outlines, font\ncollections, missing glyphs and crossing outlines are refused by name.\n\nAdd the undoable InsertOutlineText command and the MCP tool\ninsert_outline_text. The profile keeps the shapes, not the font, and\n2D operations take it as their source like a DXF profile.\n\nFixes #3072\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
