  {
    "sha": "d3b53cec9a2441d0f42a3ac82ca86321f47815d3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGQzYjUzY2VjOWEyNDQxZDBmNDJhM2FjODJjYTg2MzIxZjQ3ODE1ZDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T19:52:35Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T19:52:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(geometry): refuse nested outlines whose winding nonzero fill fills\n\nThe sketch reads holes by nesting, but a TrueType font fills by the nonzero\nwinding rule. A contour inside another that runs in the same direction is\nfilled, not a hole. Refuse that arrangement by name (OutlineTextError::Winding)\nso a pocket or cut-out never takes the wrong region.\n\nPinned by nested_outlines_follow_the_nonzero_winding_fill.\n\nRefs #3072\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
