  {
    "sha": "1646551d1bec829d01bc4b1e351644b3f5318365",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDE2NDY1NTFkMWJlYzgyOWQwMWJjNGIxZTM1MTY0NGIzZjUzMTgzNjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T09:57:13Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T09:57:13Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(text): bound composite visits, text points and glyph coordinates\n\nA hostile font must give a clean error. The reader now counts the\ncomponent visits of one glyph (MAX_PARTS 4096), so a tree of empty\nparts is refused instead of a 64^8 walk. The text charges a vertex\nbudget (MAX_VERTICES, the chainer limit) before it makes each point,\nso a large height cannot allocate gigabytes. A glyph coordinate\noutside the i16 range is refused. The decision file states that\nkerning and USE_MY_METRICS are ignored and that overlapping fonts\nare refused.\n\nRefs #3072\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "3f4c8989a31d7e46d22e5ad331ae5e6f0950d66f",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/3f4c8989a31d7e46d22e5ad331ae5e6f0950d66f"
